te one’s skills, strengths, knowledge, and experiences relevant to the position desired and career goals, and identify areas necessary for professional growth. The individual is able to navigate and explore job options, understands and can take the steps necessary to pursue opportunities, and understands how to self-advocate for opportunities in the workplace. o Equity and Inclusion: Value, respect, and learn from diverse cultures, races, ages, genders, sexual orientations, and religions. The individual demonstrates openness, inclusiveness, sensitivity, and the ability to interact respectfully with all people and understand individuals’ differences. Career Competencies Competency: Critical Thinking/Problem Solving Competency: Oral/Written Communications Competency: Teamwork/Collaboration Competency: Digital Technology Competency: Leadership Competency: Professionalism/Work Ethic Competency: Career and Self Development Competency: Equity and Inclusion Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently in good academic standing with the University? Yes No * Are you currently in good conduct standing with the University? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
