all knowingly influence others to furnish the NCAA or an ISU investigator/compliance officer false or misleading information concerning an individual’s involvement in or knowledge of matters relevant to a possible violation of an NCAA regulation. Failure to abide by this term of employment shall constitute unethical conduct as defined by the NCAA and may result in immediate suspension and/or termination of the employment relationship with ISU . Job Duties Essential Duties and Responsibilities The CAS Student Social Media Assistant helps tell the stories of the College of Arts and Sciences through engaging digital content. This position offers hands-on experience in marketing, storytelling, photography, videography, writing, and social media strategy while collaborating with the college’s marketing team. Create engaging (photo, video, graphic, written) content for the CAS social media channels and platforms. Develop and implement new ideas, identify and pitch story ideas that show showcase students, faculty, research, events, and campus life. Attend University events (including occasional evenings) to capture photos and short form videos for social media, newsletters, and other marketing materials. Assist CAS marketing team with production of internal newsletters, website updates, posters, flyers, and other marketing and communications projects. Work independently while managing assigned projects and meeting deadlines. Career Readiness Competencies o\tCritical Thinking/Problem Solving: Exercise sound reasoning to analyze issues, make decisions, and overcome problems. The individual is able to obtain, interpret, and use knowledge, facts, and data in the process, and may demonstrate originality and inventiveness. o\tOral/Written Communications: Articulate thoughts and ideas clearly and effectively in written and oral forms to persons inside and outside of the organization. The individual has public speaking skills; is able to express ideas to others; and can write/edit